{title: Shenandoah}
{artist: Traditional American}
{key: D}
{tempo: 70}
{difficulty: intermediate}
{tags: folk, shanty}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Oh [D]Shenandoah, [G]I long to [D]see you
A[Bm]way, you [G]rolling [D]river
Oh Shenan[D]doah, I [Bm]long to [G]see you
A[D]way, I'm [A]bound a[Bm]way
'Cross the [D]wide [A]Mis[D]souri

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Oh [D]Shenandoah, [G]I love your [D]daughter
A[Bm]way, you [G]rolling [D]river
For [D]her I'd [Bm]cross your [G]roaming waters
A[D]way, I'm [A]bound a[Bm]way
'Cross the [D]wide [A]Mis[D]souri
